>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `set_cond_depth`

``` hol4
simpLib.set_cond_depth : int -> simpset -> simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Sets the side-condition stack limit for invocations of a simpset.

A call to `set_cond_depth n ss` returns a copy of `ss` whose simplifier
traversals use `n` as the limit on nested conditions generated by
conditional rewrites.  A conditional rewrite is skipped when adding all
of its conditions would make the current side-condition stack longer
than `n`.  Thus, increasing the value can allow deeply nested chains of
conditional rewrites to succeed, but can also permit more work or
non-termination.

The setting is dynamically bound for each traversal.  The previous
value of `Cond_rewr.stack_limit` is restored on normal return and on an
exception, and nested simplifier invocations restore the value of their
caller.  A simpset on which `set_cond_depth` has not been called instead
uses the value of `!Cond_rewr.stack_limit` at invocation time.  That
reference is initially `4`, so existing code which changes the global
reference continues to affect unconfigured simpsets.

There is no special validation of `n`.  A value of zero rejects every
rewrite having a condition.  A negative value makes even a rewrite with
no conditions exceed the limit.

### Failure

Never fails.  Rewrites whose conditions exceed the limit are ignored;
the simplifier invocation does not fail for that reason.

### Example

The following schematic configuration gives a collection of conditional
rules room for a deeper side-condition chain without changing the
global reference.

``` hol4
val deep_ss = simpLib.set_cond_depth 40 bool_ss
val deep_tac = simpLib.SIMP_TAC deep_ss conditional_rules
```

